From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:07:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(llama-cpp): GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS, to compare a MoE
 model's expert layouts

Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0013-sycl-reorder-experts-switch.patch). ggml-sycl rewrites the
expert tensors of a mixture-of-experts model into its reorder layout at
first use. With GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS=0 they keep the layout they were
loaded in; the dense weights are reordered as before, and the default is
unchanged.

STAGED, for one comparison: a run on an Intel Arc Pro B70 with
Qwen3.6-35B-A3B whose experts had stayed in the plain layout started long
prompts about a quarter sooner at the same decode speed. Whether that is
the layout is what the switch is for
(docs/notes/backend-qualification-2026-11-21.md, the Louise repository).
Not compiled where it was written.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
---
 .../0013-sycl-reorder-experts-switch.patch    | 71 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 71 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0013-sycl-reorder-experts-switch.patch

diff --git a/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0013-sycl-reorder-experts-switch.patch b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0013-sycl-reorder-experts-switch.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c52c3df
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0013-sycl-reorder-experts-switch.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+sycl: GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS=0 leaves expert tensors in the layout they were loaded in
+
+At first use ggml-sycl rewrites each expert tensor of a mixture-of-experts
+model into the reorder (SoA) layout (opt_for_reorder_id -> reorder_qw), as
+it does the dense weights. The kernels take either layout.
+
+One run on an Intel Arc Pro B70 (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, UD-Q4_K_M, the experts
+left in the plain layout as a side effect of another experiment) started a
+2,048-token prompt in 1.80 s where the reordered model takes 2.48-2.50 s,
+and a 140-token one in 0.23-0.24 s against 0.28, at the same decode speed
+(100.8-101.1 tok/s against 100.4). One run, on memory allocated another
+way: not yet a measurement of this switch.
+
+GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS=0 skips the expert tensors' reorder and nothing
+else, so the two layouts can be compared on the same model as it normally
+runs. The default, 1, is today's behaviour.
+
+Not compiled where it was written (no SYCL compiler there).
+---
+diff --git a/docs/backend/SYCL.md b/docs/backend/SYCL.md
+index 8649fca..1045db7 100644
+--- a/docs/backend/SYCL.md
++++ b/docs/backend/SYCL.md
+@@ -840,6 +840,7 @@ User can use the device management in [docs/multi-gpu.md](https://github.com/ggm
+ | GGML_SYCL_SPARSE_FA_MARGIN | [0,..] default:256 | Set the margin value for Sparse Flash-attention.|
+ | ZES_ENABLE_SYSMAN | 0 (default) or 1 | Support to get free memory of GPU by sycl::aspect::ext_intel_free_memory.<br>Recommended to use when --split-mode = layer |
+ | UR_L0_ENABLE_RELAXED_ALLOCATION_LIMITS | 0 (default) or 1 | Allow SYCL/Unified Runtime Level Zero device allocations larger than 4 GiB. llama.cpp's direct Level Zero allocation path requests the relaxed maximum-size limit itself when GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_LEVEL_ZERO=1. |
++| GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS | 1 (default) or 0 | With 0, the expert tensors of a mixture-of-experts model (`mul_mat_id`) are not rewritten into the reorder layout at first use; the dense weights still are. To measure: on one Arc Pro B70 run of a 35B MoE at Q4_K_M the plain layout started a 2,048-token prompt sooner at the same decode speed. |
+ | GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM | 0 (default) or 1 | Enable experimental support for [USM system allocations](https://github.khronos.org/SYCL_Reference/iface/usm_basic_concept.html#system-allocations) for large GPU buffers. This requires enough host memory for model weights and caches, an Intel Xe2+ GPU such as BMG or newer and supported on Linux only, with CONFIG_DRM_XE_GPUSVM enabled. |
+ | GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK | 1 (default) or 0 | Workaround for BMG (Arc B-series) GPUs, where the Level Zero driver accepts device allocations beyond VRAM and moves the overflow to system RAM, which can exhaust host memory when a model does not fit (e.g. `-ngl 999`, see https://github.com/intel/compute-runtime/issues/1047). When enabled, a model or split buffer that does not fit in the device's free memory is refused and the model load fails with an error. Set to 0 to disable. |
+ 
+diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+index d3797f8..4f961b7 100644
+--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
++++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+@@ -147,6 +147,7 @@ int g_ggml_sycl_use_level_zero_api = 0;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_enable_flash_attention = 1;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_dev2dev_memcpy = DEV2DEV_MEMCPY_SYCL;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_usm_system = 0;
++int g_ggml_sycl_reorder_experts = 1;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_bmg_vram_check = 1;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_enable_host_pinned_mem = 1;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_host_pinned_mem_2g = 0;
+@@ -478,6 +479,7 @@ static void ggml_check_sycl() try {
+ #endif
+ 
+         g_ggml_sycl_usm_system = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM", 0);
++        g_ggml_sycl_reorder_experts = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS", 1);
+         g_ggml_sycl_bmg_vram_check = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK", 1);
+         g_ggml_sycl_enable_host_pinned_mem =
+             ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_HOST_PINNED_MEM", 1);
+@@ -617,6 +619,7 @@ static void ggml_check_sycl() try {
+ #endif
+ 
+         GGML_LOG_INFO("  GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM: %d\n", g_ggml_sycl_usm_system);
++        GGML_LOG_INFO("  GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS: %d\n", g_ggml_sycl_reorder_experts);
+         GGML_LOG_INFO("  GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK: %d\n", g_ggml_sycl_bmg_vram_check);
+         GGML_LOG_INFO("  GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_HOST_PINNED_MEM: %d\n", g_ggml_sycl_enable_host_pinned_mem);
+         GGML_LOG_INFO("  GGML_SYCL_HOST_PINNED_MEM_2G: %d\n", g_ggml_sycl_host_pinned_mem_2g);
+@@ -5090,6 +5093,11 @@ static void opt_for_reorder_id(ggml_backend_sycl_context * ctx, const ggml_tenso
+     if (!g_ggml_sycl_enable_optimize || !ctx->opt_feature.reorder) {
+         return;
+     }
++    // GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS=0: the expert tensors of a mixture-of-experts model keep the layout they were
++    // loaded in (the kernels take either); the dense weights are reordered as before
++    if (!g_ggml_sycl_reorder_experts) {
++        return;
++    }
+     if (src0->type != GGML_TYPE_Q8_0 && src0->type != GGML_TYPE_Q3_K && src0->type != GGML_TYPE_Q4_K &&
+         src0->type != GGML_TYPE_Q5_K && src0->type != GGML_TYPE_Q6_K && src0->type != GGML_TYPE_MXFP4) {
+         return;
